# Milestone: M3
# Covers: implicit tag creation at Lobby scope (t:) auto-creates a UTag; invalid
#         implicit tags (with arguments, in non-Lobby scope, composite) raise errors.
# blocked: implicit tag creation via Lobby scope lookup not implemented
# matrix-row: tag-implicit
#             and Tag.new() method dispatch)
#
# Reason:
#   Implicit tag auto-creation ('t:') requires the Lobby-level lookup fallback that
#   auto-instantiates a UTag — part of the M4 Lobby/connection infrastructure.
#   t.block() and t1.t2.block() method calls are M4.  Tag.new("t1") and related
#   named-tag construction are M4.  At M3, tag scopes require the tag to already
#   be bound in a var (e.g., var t = ...; t: {...}).
#
# Original urbiscript (activate at M4 with implicit tag and Lobby infrastructure):
# # t: detach({loop {echo("foo"); sleep(1s)}})|; [00000001] *** foo
# # sleep(2.5s); [00000002] *** foo [00000003] *** foo
# # t.block(); sleep(10ms); echo("bar"); [00000004] *** bar
# # ... (see legacy/repos/aldebaran-urbi/tests/2.x/tag/implicit.chk)
